module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.declared_type_wall_keyed_on_the_value_being_a_kernel

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { AwaitsOneGrounding, GroundingUndeclared }

data declared_type_wall_keyed_on_the_value_being_a_kernel: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "declared_type_wall_keyed_on_the_value_being_a_kernel" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: AwaitsOneGrounding { grounding: GroundingUndeclared }, trigger_capability: "an inhabitance judgment that decides from the FORMAL type's declaration for an actual value of ANY kind -- kernel, coproduct arm, record literal, alias -- SUFFICIENT FOR removing `is_kernel_type` from the guard entirely rather than adding a second relation beside it. A second relation keyed on coproducts would be the fork this row exists to prevent." } },

  receipts: [
    "**the declared-type inhabitance wall decides on the KIND OF THE OFFENDING VALUE rather than on inhabitance, so it refuses a kernel literal at a declared type and admits a WRONG COPRODUCT ARM at the same position.** DESIGN section 4b puts `values inhabit declared types` in the ordinary compiler floor, so a breach is a below-baseline safety regression and not a rung on the ladder.",

    "READ FROM THE RELATION, NOT INFERRED FROM ITS NAME. `v1.compiler.infer` `kernel_value_declared_type_mismatch_bounded` short-circuits at its second guard: `if is_kernel_type(name: actual_name) == false || actual_name == \"Unit\" { false }`. A `false` there is `no mismatch`, so an actual value whose authored name is not a kernel type leaves the relation before any formal type is consulted. Every position that consults this relation inherits that exit.",

    "WHY THIS IS NOT `one more declared-type position needs a member`, which is the natural reading and the wrong one. `test.claim.declared_type_kernel_inhabitance_witness` records that the census enumerated fourteen declared-type positions from the grammar -- every `parse_type_expr` call site in `v1.compiler.parse` -- and that seven admitted an `Int` where a coproduct was declared. Those seven were closed. But the guard above sits INSIDE the relation those positions now consult, so closing a position does nothing for a non-kernel wrong value: the record-literal field seam was ALREADY closed for kernels (that witness cites `KHold { subject: 5 }` refusing there) and still admits a wrong coproduct arm. The uncovered half is not a position, it is every position.",

    "MEASURED SPECIMEN ONE (2026-08-25, `gentle-eagle-360`, controlled fixture): with `AlphaRefusal` and `BetaRefusal` distinct coproducts and `Wrapper = WrapsBeta { cause: BetaRefusal }`, a fn returning `WrapsBeta { cause: c }` for `c: AlphaRefusal` is ACCEPTED, while the same field given an `Int` is refused and given an undeclared constructor is refused. The two refusals are what make the acceptance a measurement rather than an absence of checking.",

    "MEASURED SPECIMEN TWO (2026-09-10, gunbc#10952, found by review 63271): `data bmc_rotation_route_disposition: Disposition = SingleAuthority`, where `SingleAuthority` is an arm of `ConstructionMechanism` and `Disposition` declares only `Terminal` and `Scaffold`. It rode FOUR GREEN REQUIRED CHECKS. Two independent observations that it compiled rather than being skipped: a `gunbc run` over that closure resolved it and failed only on a wrong function name, and the pull request was green on all four required checks with the row present.",

    "MEASURED SPECIMEN THREE (2026-09-22, main ff2110b7e24, `quiet-ibex-229` from a `neat-boar-16` measurement, discovered by `loyal-swift-608` while demoting `lively-bat-737`'s construction wall): A COLLECTION AND A NOMINAL PRODUCT WERE MUTUALLY ADMITTED AT A DECLARED POSITION, IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. THE SIX-CELL GRID, each cell one `gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --source-root <probe> --entry <probe>.dag --function probe` over a one-module fixture. ADMITTED, body ran and returned: `type Rec { a: String }` with `fn takes_rec(r: Rec)` given `fn a_list() -> List<String>`; and the dual, `fn takes_list(xs: List<Int>)` given `fn a_rec() -> Rec`. REFUSED, so the direct-call seam demonstrably runs on these fixtures: `Int <- String`, `Int <- List<Int>`, `Rec <- Other` (a second record), `Rec <- Optional<Int>`. The two admissions are therefore a hole in the relation, not an unreached position.",

    "THE CHAIN FOR SPECIMEN THREE, re-derived per DESIGN section 6b rather than patched at the symptom. `v1.compiler.infer` `declared_type_inhabitance`, declared=`Rec`, produced=`List<String>`: the optional arm does not fire; declared is not generic; both names resolve; `declared_realizes_as_kernel_numeric` no; `collection_at_scalar_declared_type` REFUSES ONLY WHEN THE DECLARED BASE PEELS TO A KERNEL SCALAR and `Rec` does not, so false; `record_at_scalar_needs_identity` wants a kernel declared, no; `coproduct_at_record_declared_type` wants a coproduct produced, no; `refinement_inhabitance` Absent; `kernel_value_declared_type_mismatch` false because the actual is not a kernel -- THE EXACT GUARD THIS ROW NAMES; `coproduct_payload_where_parent_required` no; `nominal_product_inhabitance_refusal` asks `nominal_product_head_name(produced)`, which answers the empty string for a collection BY DESIGN, so none. The relation then reaches its TERMINAL ARM, `Inhabits`, BY FALLTHROUGH. The dual falls through the same way with the roles swapped. THE EARLIEST UNJUSTIFIED BOUNDARY is that the relation's terminal arm is ACCEPTANCE while no arm ever judged collection-versus-nominal-product disjointness: every arm keys on the kind of ONE side, which is this row's recognition rule seen in a second vocabulary -- `is_kernel_type` on the actual is one instance of it and `node_is_collection` on the produced is another.",

    "WHAT SPECIMEN THREE'S REPAIR IS, AND WHAT IT IS NOT. gunbc#12045 replaces `collection_at_scalar_declared_type` with `collection_versus_established_identity`, a RELATION BETWEEN THE TWO SIDES: exactly one side is an element or keyed collection after `expand_nominal_alias_rhs` on BOTH sides, and the other side is an ESTABLISHED non-generic identity -- kernel scalar, nominal product or coproduct by `expected_type_head_exposure`. It is a replacement rather than a sibling arm precisely because a second relation keyed on products is the fork this row exists to prevent. THAT IS STILL NOT THIS ROW'S NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER. The trigger names ONE JUDGMENT FROM THE FORMAL'S DECLARATION FOR AN ACTUAL OF ANY KIND, sufficient for removing the offending-value guards entirely; the repair removes one such guard and leaves `kernel_value_declared_type_mismatch` and the head-name arms standing. The row stays open, and a future change may retire it only by landing exactly the trigger.",

    "HARM, AND IT IS THE SECOND SPECIMEN THAT SHOWS THE SHAPE. The review that found it concluded `the module therefore does not compile, and with it the whole witness closure` -- reasonable, and false. So the defect does not merely admit a wrong value: it makes a reader who assumes the floor holds derive a WRONG CONSEQUENCE from a correct observation. The author had four green checks saying the row was fine and a reviewer saying the module was absent, and neither was true.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: this is NOT the evidence-overreach family (a receipt supporting more than its instrument established) -- nothing here is a receipt, and the claim is not about coverage. It is NOT `check_subject_shape_cannot_represent_the_state_the_check_detects` -- the relation can represent the state perfectly; it declines to look. The tell is a wall whose guard names a property of the OFFENDING VALUE (`is_kernel_type`) where the property under test is a RELATION between the value and its declared type.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the floor, which is not a rung. The class is decidable and the authority exists -- `lookup_type_by_name` and the declared-type env are already in hand at the guard that exits -- so this is DESIGN section 5's `wall after grounding` with the grounding already present. CEILING: structurally guaranteed; a wrong-typed literal is authorable in source, so impossibility is not available, but no `Accepted` program need contain one. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMED AS A CAPABILITY: an inhabitance judgment that decides from the FORMAL type's declaration for an actual value of ANY kind -- kernel, coproduct arm, record literal, alias -- SUFFICIENT FOR removing `is_kernel_type` from the guard entirely rather than adding a second relation beside it. A second relation keyed on coproducts would be the fork this row exists to prevent.",

    "MEASURED SPECIMEN FOUR (2026-09-24, reported by lane `bold-raven-671` against a private specimen, reproduced by `keen-stag-684` on public main cfb9ff8): a NULLARY FOREIGN ARM at the data-initializer and declared-return positions. Fixture: `type FvAlpha = FvX | FvY`, `type FvBeta = FvZ | FvW`, `data fv_v: FvBeta = FvX`, `fn fv_ret() -> FvBeta { FvX }`. INTERPRETER (`gunbc run`): a fn declared `-> FvBeta` returning `fv_v` evaluated to an FvAlpha, and a total match over FvBeta's two arms died with `PatternMatchFailure { value: \"FvX\" }`. EMIT ROUTE (`gunbc compile --target rust`): `compiled: 6 files emitted, 0 diagnostics`, emitting `pub fn fv_ret() -> FvBeta { FvAlpha::FvX }` -- the refusal deferred to rustc, which is outside the modeled guarantee.",

    "THE CHAIN FOR SPECIMEN FOUR, per DESIGN section 6b. The bare arm's inferred type is correct: `variant_reference_inferred_node` keeps the owner the binder chose (FvAlpha) because the expected FvBeta does not own FvX, so the reference link is justified. Both positions then reach `declared_type_conformance_diags`, which judged ground kernels, ground element collections, nominal products and callables, and had NO ARM for a coproduct pair -- while `coproduct_payload_where_parent_required`, the relation the record-literal field seam and `declared_type_inhabitance` already consult for exactly this pair, sat unconsulted there. That seam is the earliest unjustified boundary for these two positions. REPAIR: `declared_type_conformance_diags` consumes `coproduct_payload_where_parent_required` -- the existing relation at two more positions, no new relation. RED and positive control: `test.claim.declared_type_foreign_variant_witness` (a foreign arm refused at both positions; the native arm accepted at both), in the required gate by the `test.claim.declared_type_` prefix; the two refusing members return false on the pre-change binary and true after.",

    "SPECIMEN FOUR'S BLAST RADIUS, ENUMERATED BY IDENTITY AND FIXED FORWARD, NOT EXEMPTED. The instrument is a differential of the whole-corpus covering compile (`gunbc compile --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --target rust --repository gunbc --measured-root-demands tools/whole_corpus_compile_measured_root_demands.json`) run with the pre-repair and post-repair binaries: the sorted blocking `error[..]` lines of each, compared, name every newly refused site by file and position. On main cfb9ff8 the repair newly refused 67 sites in two groups. GROUP ONE, SPECIMEN TWO'S SHAPE (63): `data <name>: Disposition = SingleAuthority` rows in production modules, the planted nullary fixture `test.fixture.decl_facts_reflection.specimens` `planted_nullary_disposition_specimen` of the same shape, and that module's `mechanism_data_ref`, declared `ConstructionMechanism` but initialised with the Disposition arm `Terminal`. Fixed forward by retyping each SingleAuthority row's annotation to the type its value inhabits (`ConstructionMechanism`) and by initialising `mechanism_data_ref` with `RealizationDispatch`; the production rows have no consumer outside their own files, and the two fixture rows keep the shape their witnesses assert (a top-level nullary arm named SingleAuthority; a coproduct-typed data reference that is not a variant value). Specimen two was therefore not one row but a population that four green checks never saw. GROUP TWO, PAYLOAD WHERE PARENT REQUIRED (4): functions declared `-> ContentHash` whose body returns the bare `Fnv1a64Structural` payload of `content_hash_atom` -- `v2.compiler.emit_host` `emit_host_string_list_digest`, `test.claim.roadmap.roadmap_static_site_witness` `fixture_site_artifact_digest`, `gunbc.host.host_identity_adopt` `host_identity_adopt_model_hash`, `gunbc.host.host_identity_assimilation` `host_identity_assimilation_model_hash`. Fixed forward at the consumer's declared type: the first two feed `Fnv1a64Structural` fields (`std.artifact_store` `ArtifactRealizationInput.content_digest`, the roadmap artifact `digest`), so their returns are retyped; the last two feed `ContentHash` `model_hash` fields, so their values are wrapped with `std.content_hash` `as_content_hash_structural`. After both groups the post-repair blocking set equals the pre-repair set line for line.",

    "WHAT SPECIMEN FOUR'S REPAIR IS NOT: this row's trigger. It adds a consumer of an existing arm at two positions; it does not remove `is_kernel_type` from any guard, and the relation it consumes still excludes GENERIC coproducts and compares arm NAME SETS rather than declaration identity. The positional next step is wiring `PositionDataInitializer` and `PositionDeclaredReturn` as `DeclaredTypeObligation` producers into `declared_type_obligation_diags`, so these positions consult the ONE relation rather than a hand-picked arm of it; the row's capability trigger stands unchanged.",

    "NOT CLAIMED HERE: how many of the fourteen positions admit a wrong coproduct. The guard's placement implies all of them, and I did not measure them one at a time. A census across the fourteen positions is not owed: that prerequisite is retired by the 2026-10-30 process ruling (`gunbc.design_ruling bad_process_is_worse_than_no_process`), which does not establish coverage of them; a position is checked with a focused witness when a change touches it.",

    "MEASURED SPECIMEN FIVE (2026-10-17, pinned pair b97793f4603b / f907616774e, `fierce-fox-568`, node://adhoc-ed047a8d-5b3; the shape was first measured on the shipped seed binary by `gentle-carp-16` as a probe for gunbc#14152): A BOOL VARIABLE WAS ACCEPTED AT A SCALAR FORMAL WHILE THE BOOL LITERAL AT THE SAME FORMAL REFUSED. `fn takes(x: Int) -> Int { x }` plus `fn probe(q: Bool) -> Int { takes(x: q) }` compiled with ZERO blocking diagnostics (the harness filter is `v1_compiler_infer_env::is_interpreter_blocking_diagnostic`; not even a warning survived), while `takes(x: true)` refused `value does not inhabit its declared type at the direct call argument for parameter 'x': declared 'Primitive(Int)', produced 'Primitive(Bool)'`. The same asymmetry at the declared-return (`fn probe(q: Bool) -> Int { q }` accepted, `{ true }` refused), the record field (`Box { n: q }` accepted for `type Box { n: Int }`) and the let annotation. THE ARGUMENT-INHABITANCE JUDGMENT DEMONSTRABLY RUNS ON THESE FIXTURES -- the same fixture shape with a P-at-Q coproduct pair refuses, as do record-at-Int and String-at-Int -- so this is a hole in the relation, not an unreached position. THE HARM IS INTERPRETATION, NOT ONLY EMISSION: with `fn takes(x: Int) -> Int { x }`, `fn probe(q: Bool) -> Int { takes(x: q) }` and `fn entry() -> Int { probe(q: true) }`, the compile reported graph:true with zero blocking diagnostics and the INTERPRETER answered `Bool(true)` at an entry declared to return Int; the emitted Rust carried `fn probe(q:bool) -> i64 { takes(x: q) }` -- not type-correct Rust, so a module inside a cargo-built emitted closure cannot be carrying this today, and the only required lane that emits a retained closure and cargo-builds it (`//gunbc/instruments:emitted-subject-build-gate`, two subjects) was shown clean by the census below.",

    "THE CHAIN FOR SPECIMEN FIVE, per DESIGN section 6b -- AND IT IS THIS ROW'S RECOGNITION RULE IN A THIRD VOCABULARY, AT A GUARD THIS ROW DID NOT YET NAME. `v1.compiler.infer` `kernel_value_declared_type_mismatch_bounded` had TWO value-kind gates, not one. This row names the second (`is_kernel_type(actual_name) == false || Unit` admits). The FIRST bail was `formal.connective == Arrow || actual.connective == Arrow || (actual_base.children |> count) > 0` -- a bail keyed on the RUNTIME SHAPE (child count) of the produced node inside a relation whose judgment is about the DECLARED type. The corpus Bool is `type Bool = True | False`, so a Bool VARIABLE's node carries two children and the relation answered `no mismatch` before any comparison, while the `true` literal is a childless kernel spelling and reaches the kernel mismatch -- one judgment, two verdicts for one declared type, decided by the value's spelling. THE EARLIEST UNJUSTIFIED BOUNDARY is that first bail: nothing in DESIGN 4b makes childlessness a qualification for inhabitance judgment, and every acceptance it actually produced was either refused by a cited name-level judgment elsewhere or is an admit this row already tracks. REPAIR (gunbc session/fierce-fox-568): the children-count term is WITHDRAWN; the produced side is judged by its declared head name through the exemptions the relation already owns -- name equality, the declared `dag_can_cast` rows (Int<->Float) and the grounded identity rows (Int->Nat, String->FreeMonoid in `dag/std/coercion.dag`), the structural-carrier template, the single-child refinement. EIGHT SHAPES FLIPPED ACCEPTED -> REFUSED on the pinned pair, all Bool-shaped: the Bool variable at the direct call argument, the declared return, the record field, the let annotation; Bool at a Float formal; Bool at `FreeMonoid<Int>`; `FreeMonoid<Bool>` at `FreeMonoid<Int>` (refused `at the generic type argument`); and the harm chain. Every other shape of the 26-shape matrix is unchanged, and each surviving acceptance carries a cited route.",

    "WHAT SPECIMEN FIVE'S REPAIR IS NOT: this row's trigger. The `is_kernel_type(actual_name)` guard still stands -- a value whose declared head is NOT kernel-named leaves before the formal is consulted. Measured unchanged on both sides of the pin: a user `type Nat = Zero | Succ { predecessor: Nat }` at an Int formal, a user `type Opt<T>` at an Int formal, and a user coproduct at an Int formal all remain ACCEPTED -- each exits through the `is_kernel_type` guard, which is exactly this row's named next rung. (The reverse Nat shape, an Int value at a declared `Nat` formal, is accepted separately at the name comparison by the grounded Int->Nat identity row -- a cited route, not an exit.) The row stays open, and its named trigger -- one judgment from the formal's declaration for an actual of ANY kind, removing the offending-value guards entirely -- is unchanged by this repair. BLAST RADIUS, by the same instrument as specimen four's (whole-corpus covering compile, `gunbc compile --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --target rust --repository gunbc --measured-root-demands tools/whole_corpus_compile_measured_root_demands.json`, sorted blocking `error[..]` lines compared): ZERO newly refused modules -- 13 inhabitance refusals at the parent and 13 at the fix, byte-identical, with the pins printed inside each dispatch (the shared runner workspace drifted once mid-campaign, which is why both legs now checkout explicit commits and echo `git rev-parse HEAD`). `v2.std.inhabitance` refuses the same shape (measured by `gunbc run` over a v2 fixture: boolvar=refused, bool_literal=refused, product=refused, coproduct_pair=refused, green=inhabits); v2 is not implicated.",
    "ONE CELL OF THE CENSUS ABOVE LIVES AT ANOTHER ROW: a nominal product given by reference at a record-literal field declared as a kernel scalar is accepted because this row's `is_kernel_type` guard exits first; the measurement and the rung correction are at `product_value_at_a_scalar_formal_is_accepted`, which owns the class. This row's capability trigger is unchanged.",

    "CARET/SYMBOL SPECIMEN, CONDITIONAL -- ITS PREMISE IS NOT YET MAIN (folded 2026-10-20; each assertion re-derived from source). `std.syntax` declares the Symbol literal `LitSymbol { value: String }` (dag/std/syntax.dag; the caret lowering to it is MQ-1), and `v1.compiler.infer_types.infer_literal_node` today assigns `LitSymbol { value: _ } => string_type` -- so `fn f() -> String { ^tag }` is simply typed String and the caret reaches no Symbol position. The unjudged-inhabitance reading becomes live ONLY when that literal arm yields a Symbol, and is recorded here so the moment is not missed. WHY THIS ROW AND NOT THE OPAQUE ROW: the declared position here is the KERNEL `String`, and the escape that would admit a Symbol-typed actual at it is this row's own guard -- `kernel_value_declared_type_mismatch_bounded` (v1.compiler.infer) short-circuits on `if is_kernel_type(name: actual_name) == false || actual_name == \"Unit\" { false }` BEFORE the formal name is derived and compared (that derivation is the next let, inside the guard's else branch), so an actual whose authored name is outside `std.types.kernel_type_set` -- which contains no Symbol row -- is never compared at all. That is this row's named nonkernel-actual escape, and the specimen is one more actual-kind of its trigger, which stands unchanged: one judgment from the formal's declaration for an actual of ANY kind. THE CONVERSION DIRECTION IS THE OPPOSITE OF THE OPAQUE SPECIMEN'S: this crossing would be Symbol -> String, for which `v2.std.node` already declares `symbol_lexeme` (sym: Symbol) -> String -- the reverse crossing (String -> Symbol, `symbol_intern_lexeme`) belongs to the opaque specimen at `a_value_of_any_type_is_admitted_at_an_opaque_declared_type`. The caret's literal typing is owned by #14082, not here; fixing the arm establishes nothing about this class.",

    "MEASURED SPECIMEN SEVEN (2026-10-24, `bold-ant-48`, node://adhoc-4789e04c-ca5; reported by `tidy-ant-251` from a `zesty-badger-599` measurement on a seed built from 5f9c6779e9e): STRUCTURED VALUES AT THE KERNEL-NAMED, KERNEL-GROUNDED COPRODUCT `std.integer` `Int`, AT THE DIRECT CALL ARGUMENT. Re-measured on a seed built from a81d823324f (`gunbc --version` prints it), one `gunbc compile --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --source-root docs/measurements/direct_call_structured_value_at_int/dag --entry <probe> --target dag` per probe, the seven probe modules held on the never-merge branch `probe/bold-ant-48-direct-call-structured-value-at-int` at 24f8c0da3cbd (not in the corpus); each probe module is one fn calling `std.integer` `int_to_decimal_string(value:)`. ACCEPTED, 0 blocking: a record parameter (`gunbc.dcs_record_red`, `type DcsRecord { mark: DcsMark }`), a local coproduct parameter (`gunbc.dcs_variant_red`, `type DcsLocal = DcsOne | DcsTwo`) and a nullary local variant literal (`gunbc.dcs_variant_literal_red`). REFUSED, so the seam runs on these fixtures: a `std.types` `Bool` parameter (`gunbc.dcs_bool_control`), twice -- `type mismatch: expected Coproduct(Int), got Coproduct(Bool)` and `value does not inhabit its declared type at the direct call argument for parameter value`. ACCEPTED as they must be: an `Int` parameter, the literal `7`, and `NonNegative { n: n }` (`gunbc.dcs_int_positive`, `dcs_int_literal_positive`, `dcs_int_arm_positive`). HARM, per the report: the interpreter dies later, `cannot apply Lt to Record and Int`, inside the callee -- a refusal located in the wrong function, at run time.",

    "THE CHAIN FOR SPECIMEN SEVEN, read from `v1.compiler.infer` `declared_type_inhabitance`, per DESIGN section 6b -- THIS ROW'S RECOGNITION RULE ON THE DECLARED SIDE. Declared is `std.integer` `Int` (`NonNegative { n: Nat } | Negative { pred: Nat }`), a corpus coproduct whose spelling is a kernel name. Produced `DcsRecord`: `product_at_scalar_declared_type` declines because the declared head exposes as a coproduct, not a kernel scalar; `product_versus_coproduct_head_mismatch` is the arm that owns a product at a coproduct, but `nominal_coproduct_head_name` answers the empty string for any name with `is_kernel_type(name)`, so the declared coproduct head is ERASED by its spelling and the arm cannot fire; `kernel_value_declared_type_mismatch` exits because the actual is not kernel-named (the guard this row names); `nominal_product_inhabitance_refusal` asks for a declared product and gets none. The relation reaches its terminal `Inhabits` by fallthrough. Produced `DcsLocal`: no arm judges two distinct non-generic coproducts at all (specimen five already recorded a user coproduct at Int accepted). Bool refuses only because ITS spelling is kernel-named on the produced side. The same kernel-spelling exclusion sits in `nominal_product_head_name`. So the guard keyed on a kernel SPELLING is not only on the offending value: it also erases the declared identity of every corpus declaration that carries a kernel name (Int, Nat, Bool, String), which is the state the row's trigger names -- a judgment from the formal's declaration, not from either side's spelling.",

    "CORRECTION FOR SPECIMEN SEVEN, PER DESIGN SECTION 7 (the seed is a regression oracle, never a specification): THE NATIVE v2 ROUTE REFUSES WHAT THE SEED ADMITS, SO THIS IS A SEED DEFECT v2 DOES NOT CARRY FORWARD. Measured 2026-10-24 on BuildBuddy (48 GB runner) at a81d823324f: the seed built, `gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:v2-native-census-scoped` emitted and cargo-built the native driver (`gunbc-emitted-closure-src-v2-compiler-source-root-eval-dag`), and that binary ran `census-scoped //gunbc/<probe>:all dag src/v2` once per probe, the seven probe modules copied into `dag/gunbc/` on the runner because the native route binds only the layout roots (a third root refuses `native_lane_source_roots_refused`). REFUSED at infer, `fatal_reason: application_argument_does_not_inhabit` (v2.std.inhabitance), each a closed 30-member scope: `gunbc.dcs_record_red`, `gunbc.dcs_variant_red`, `gunbc.dcs_variant_literal_red`, and the `gunbc.dcs_bool_control` control. INFERRED (accepted, advisories only, `infer_grounding_not_derived`): `gunbc.dcs_int_positive`, `gunbc.dcs_int_literal_positive`, `gunbc.dcs_int_arm_positive`. WHY v2 DECIDES IT: `v2.std.inhabitance` `inhabitance_declaration_heads_differ` compares the two sides' DECLARATION heads and `declared_type_inhabitance_exact` compares by exact structural equality; neither consults a spelling, so the kernel-named declaration `std.integer` `Int` keeps its identity. NO SEED REPAIR (gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing purpose test): no v2 self-host path depends on the seed admitting these pairs -- a module that did would be refused by the native route measured here -- so changing v1 here would serve no v2 program. This row's seed rung, ceiling and capability trigger are unchanged; the correction is that the native route already holds this cell. Reproduction, at that branch head: build the seed; run `gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:v2-native-census-scoped` and copy the driver it emits under its private probe root (`target/release/gunbc-emitted-closure-src-v2-compiler-source-root-eval-dag`, removed when the run ends) before the run finishes; copy the probes into `dag/gunbc/`; then per probe `<driver> census-scoped //gunbc/<probe>:all dag src/v2` and read the probe's `cause_group` `fatal_reason` (refused) or its `native-census-infer` `outcome` (`inferred` is accepted). One `ctrl-build --remote` dispatch on a 48 GB runner holds both routes.",
    "MEASURED SPECIMEN, ANONYMOUS TUPLE ELEMENT (2026-10-25, smart-tern-402, found while measuring a seed slot-spelling repair for gunbc#15115; routed by keen-heron-809; the same family gunbc#15127 extends): a collection whose ELEMENT is the seed's anonymous tuple (v1.compiler.infer_types make_tuple_type: name empty, no span, Conj of first/second; the enumerate template's element) is ADMITTED at a declared collection position whatever the declared element is. Seed built from 557a7efac39 (sha256 0a7df0fccc50550532fc817e6fd9f393f63b157e2ecadf78c22d4e17fda2ffcd), each a separate module compiled by gunbc run: `fn want_strings(xs: List<String>) -> Int { 0 }` with `want_strings(xs: ys |> enumerate)` for `ys: List<String>` is ACCEPTED, and `fn same_element<T>(xs: FreeMonoid<T>, probe: T) -> Bool` with `same_element(xs: ys |> enumerate, probe: 3)` is ACCEPTED. The controls that make those accepts wrong refuse: `want_strings(xs: ys |> map(y => 1))` refuses \"value does not inhabit its declared type at the generic type argument: declared 'Primitive(String)', produced 'Primitive(Int)'\", and `want_strings(xs: [1, 2])` refuses with a type mismatch. So a NAMED wrong element is judged and an anonymous one is not: the anonymous tuple has no spelling to compare, which is the not-ground reading that falls through to admission (declared_type_conformance_diags_core `if !both_ground { [] }`, the shape gunbc#15127 records).",

    "v2 STANDING FOR THE ANONYMOUS TUPLE ELEMENT: OUTSIDE v2'S CURRENT REACH, NOT REFUSED BY v2. The class has no v2 constructor, so v2 neither admits nor refuses it, and nothing here is evidence that v2 judges it. TRIGGER THAT MAKES IT TESTABLE: v2 gaining an `enumerate` declaration or a tuple production (a tuple type or literal); at that point the anonymous-element arms of v2.test.claim.anonymous_tuple_element_inhabitance must be rewritten to construct the element and assert the refusal, and until then the seed defect stays open with no v2 counterpart. Under DESIGN section 7 the seed is not patched (no v2 path depends on it, so it does not block v2 corpus authoring). Stated as unconstructible, not refused, because that is what was measured (review 86023 caught the first version of this receipt claiming a refusal its fixture never exercised): v2.test.claim.anonymous_tuple_element_inhabitance shows v2 has no anonymous tuple at all -- `enumerate` has no declaration to bind (resolve refuses resolve_reason_unbound_symbol) and the grammar has no tuple production (a tuple type, and separately a tuple literal, each refuses at parse with parse_g0_tokens_remain in its own fixture), each beside an accepted one-term control that differs only there. The nearest element v2 can write is a DECLARED product, and at both seed positions it is judged: Seq<Pair<Int, Bool>> refuses with application_argument_does_not_inhabit where Seq<Bool> is declared and where a generic's element is fixed at Int by another argument, with one-variable controls accepted. That second half is the named-element case the seed ALSO judges: it shows the floor holding in v2 for a declared product and is NOT coverage of the anonymous route. Executed by v2.test.claim.anonymous_tuple_element_inhabitance (gunbc run --claim-run). The seed side stays in this row's open population.",

    "MEASURED SPECIMEN EIGHT (2026-10-25, `sleek-wren-845`, node://adhoc-6c51066f-59a; reported by `tidy-ant-251` from a `warm-crane-888` probe build at 88e8991e557): A WRONG DECLARED RETURN WHOSE PRODUCED HEAD IS SPELLED THROUGH A TRANSPARENT ALIAS. The report was `fn pas_only_m(m: Map<String, Int>) -> FinitelySupportedFunction<String, Int> { m }`, accepted with no detector firing. That probe is CORRECTLY accepted: `std.types` declares `type Map<key, value> = FinitelySupportedFunction<key, value>`, so the two sides are one type. What it hid is measured with a discriminating set, one `gunbc compile --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --source-root <probe root> --entry <probe>` per probe on a seed built from 88e8991e557 (the probes are not in the corpus; a typecheck pass is read as 0 `error` rows, since the emitted-workspace step after it refuses these single-module entries with `EmitterReverseEdge`, which is not a typecheck verdict). REFUSED, one located type mismatch at the body: Bool at a declared Int, a record `A` at an unrelated record `B`, a coproduct `C` at an unrelated coproduct `D`, and three type-argument mismatches whose heads are spelled alike on both sides -- `Fsf<Int, Bool>` at `Fsf<Int, Int>`, `List<Bool>` at `List<String>`, `FreeMonoid<Bool>` at `FreeMonoid<String>`. ACCEPTED WITH 0 BLOCKING, and wrong: `List<Bool>` at `FreeMonoid<String>`, `Map<String, Int>` at `FinitelySupportedFunction<String, String>`, and, with a user alias `type M<K, V> = Fsf<K, V>`, `M<Int, Bool>` at `Fsf<Int, Int>`. ACCEPTED and right (controls): Int at Int, `A` at `A`, `A` at a transparent alias `B = A`, `List<Bool>` at `FreeMonoid<Bool>`, `Map<String, Int>` at `FinitelySupportedFunction<String, Int>`, `M<Int, Bool>` at `Fsf<Int, Bool>`. So the type arguments are judged exactly when the two heads are SPELLED alike, and an alias spelling on one side lets any argument through.",

    "THE CHAIN FOR SPECIMEN EIGHT, read from `v1.compiler.infer`, per DESIGN section 6b. A declared return is judged by `declared_type_conformance_diags_core`, a chain of refusal detectors ending in `else if !both_ground { [] }`: a pair no detector recognizes is ADMITTED, not judged (the admit-by-default the report named). The detector that owns an applied-argument conflict between two nominal products is `nominal_product_inhabitance_refusal`, which reaches `applied_type_arguments_conflict` only when `nominal_product_head_name` names a declared product on BOTH sides. That function reads the AUTHORED spelling (`authored_name_at`) and answers the empty string for a kernel-spelled name, an element collection or a keyed collection before it consults any declaration, so for `List<Bool>` and `Map<String, Int>` the detector abstains (`none`), the remaining detectors do not own the pair, neither side is a ground kernel scalar or ground element collection (`conformance_ground_type`), and the chain returns `[]`. The user-alias pair takes a different link: `nominal_product_head_name_if_declared_product` peels a transparent alias, so `M` is a non-empty product head and the pair reaches `nominal_product_heads_agree` and `applied_type_arguments_conflict`; WHICH link of that argument scan abstains for `M<Int, Bool>` while it refuses the same arguments under `Fsf<Int, Bool>` was NOT ISOLATED (read from source, not traced), so it is stated as observed behavior only. Earliest unjustified boundary, for the collection pairs: alignment of two applications keyed on their spelling rather than on the declarations they denote after alias unfolding -- the same `nominal_product_head_name` spelling exclusion specimen seven names, read at the return position -- beneath a chain whose terminal arm admits what no detector owns. FAMILY, so whoever retires the root sees every instance: the argument position of the same root is `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode` `list_typed_value_element_mismatch_admitted` specimen two (gunbc#15117, `merry-deer-485`: `direct_call_generic_type_argument_inhabitance_diags` builds type-argument obligations only when the two heads are spelled alike), and a `FreeMonoid<T>` formal not instantiated from a `List` argument (lanes `bold-koi-381` and `smart-tern-402`) is the unification instance; that one gets a seed patch because it blocks v2 corpus authoring. NOT CLAIMED: that these are the only detectors that abstain on an alias spelling, or the other declared positions (data initializer, record field) for these pairs; only the declared return was measured.",

    "CORRECTION FOR SPECIMEN EIGHT, PER DESIGN SECTION 7 (the seed is a regression oracle, never a specification): v2 DECIDES EVERY ONE OF THESE RETURNS BY A POSITIVE JUDGMENT, SO THIS IS A SEED DEFECT v2 DOES NOT CARRY FORWARD. `v2.compiler.infer` `infer_arrow_declared_return_check` builds one PositionDeclaredReturn obligation per bodied Arrow through `infer_judge_declared_position`, the judge every argument and record field meets. It alias-normalizes both sides (`infer_type_alias_normalized_at`, at the head and inside every Instantiation argument), and `v2.std.inhabitance` `declared_type_inhabitance` answers Inhabits only with a `find_witness` exact-structural-equality witness; a pair no rule witnesses is refused. There is no detector set to fall through. ROUTE CLAIMS, `v2.test.claim.compiler.infer_declared_return_source_witness` (authored source through `v2.test.claim.body_let_annotation` `bla_assemble_with_peers`, then `infer`), all twelve PASS under `gunbc run` of a scratch driver on the seed built from 88e8991e557. Each red carries `arrow_body_does_not_inhabit_declared_return`. Each control is Accepted with every diagnostic in an allow-list (`infer_grounding_not_derived`), i.e. decided Inhabits rather than counted. The predicate fails closed, so an undecidable reason added later fails a control rather than reading as decided. Two further claims keep that red authorable: a fold-callback return and a return spelled as the fn's own type variable, both Accepted but counted undecidable, are refused by the predicate. MUTATION, so the route and not only the answer is established: with `declared_type_inhabitance_exact` answering Inhabits on a `find_witness` Rejected, all five reds go red and all five controls stay green. THE EMITTED NATIVE ROUTE AGREES. Measured 2026-10-25 on BuildBuddy (48 GB runner, invocation a2c006d0-2607-4529-a161-6776ebec1ddd) at main 557a7efac39 with this change applied (the five commits past 88e8991e557 touch none of v2.compiler.infer, v2.std.inhabitance or v1.compiler.infer): the seed built, `gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:v2-native-census-scoped` emitted and cargo-built the native driver, and, by specimen seven's recipe, that driver ran `census-scoped //gunbc/<probe>:all dag src/v2` once per probe with the fifteen probes copied into `dag/gunbc/` on the runner. Each run completed over a closed scope. All nine wrong returns -- the six seed-refused pairs and the three the seed admits -- are `infer_refused` with fatal reason `arrow_body_does_not_inhabit_declared_return`; all six controls are `inferred`. NO SEED REPAIR (gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing purpose test): no v2 self-host path depends on the seed admitting these pairs -- a module that did would be refused by the v2 route measured here -- so changing v1 here would serve no v2 program. The seed-side positive identity is Charter 1 item 3 (gunbc#15091, `sunny-deer-180`); its shadow count sits at `nominal_product_heads_agree`, which these pairs never reach, as that lane was told. This row's seed rung, ceiling and capability trigger are unchanged.",

    "RE-MEASUREMENT OF SPECIMEN SEVEN, RECORD ARM (zesty-badger-599, seed 747ed06b from f20cdcc799ee, tree 761485283f2f; srv1 ~/zb-evidence/k7.log sha256 741b255780039b4db5266c0d0a6be20705183f4646df2e68bc63733c414ab933; fixtures zz_k_record.dag 3c32ce6b86228c525c7e9ca5686097f9f1c140bccdc8d7a1d4e81fa6e5fd2b31, zz_k_control.dag 2d48078a76c3448e55db3886e2da2a98d011d9e8e65db41c3514147ecd7fb86e): a record `ZzR { a: Int }` at a kernel Int parameter is ADMITTED and fails at runtime, 'cannot apply Lt to Record and Int'; Bool and String already refuse at resolve. The coproduct arm was withdrawn by the finder (the fixture cannot tell std.integer Int from the kernel Int). No new row. RED and control, unrun: `test.claim.record_argument_at_int_parameter_witness`.",

    "SPECIMEN: RIGID TYPE PARAMETER AT A KERNEL Int (zesty-badger-599, same seed, tree and k7.log as the record re-measurement above; fixture zz_k_generic.dag f0893c8060c853838099c52a8b22218e8dfb26d01a89165a4a581579f92609b3): `fn zz_m<T>(v: T)` passing v to an Int parameter is ADMITTED. FOLDED INTO THIS ROW, NOT A NEW CLASS (DESIGN section 6b root generalization, ruling keen-heron-809): record, rigid T and probably Char (candidate (b) of an_int_argument_inhabits_a_nat_parameter_at_typecheck) reach ONE mechanism, the terminal default of `v1.compiler.infer` `declared_type_inhabitance` answering Inhabits; a judgment whose last arm is acceptance is the DESIGN section 5 fail-open. The generalized repair is that one terminal arm (refuse, or a typed undecided where the facts are undecidable), NOT a produced-is-generic arm beside the kernel arm, which would be the next leaf. A rigid parameter never inhabits a concrete kernel type, so the case is decidable. CAVEAT, UNRUN: if `authored_name_at` of T is empty, the route is the UndecidableProducedIdentityErased advisory rather than the terminal arm; a run settles which. Not #15441's frontier (no concrete sibling position). RED and control, unrun: `test.claim.generic_parameter_at_int_parameter_witness`.",
